---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: help.pages
  size: 1
  alias: entry
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ entry.edition.prefix }}/help/{{ entry.guide.slug }}/"
# In the collections since #535: the layout's hreflang links and the footer
# switcher derive a page's twins from the build's own page list, and a guide
# page now has one. Nothing else reads the guides from a collection.
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ entry.guide.title }}"
  seoTitle: "{{ entry.guide.seoTitle }}"
  description: "{{ entry.guide.description }}"
---
{#
  One help guide, on its own URL (#166) — in every language the studio holds
  it in (#535).

  ── why this page exists ──
  #136 put all eleven guides into the served HTML, which fixed the real bug: a
  crawler used to be handed the word "Loading…". But it put them on ONE URL, and
  a URL is the unit Google ranks. "Sharing a pitch" and "Workspace settings,
  members, billing" answer different questions and were competing as a single
  24,000-pixel page, which meant neither could be the result for either question.

  ── the objection on the board row, and the answer ──
  The row asked to wait for #137's Search Console data. That evidence cannot
  exist while the guides share a URL — Search Console reports per URL, so it
  can no more attribute an impression to a guide than the page can rank for one.
  And these pages are DERIVED from the corpus, so there is no per-guide judgment
  left for data to inform: the studio's docs decide what exists here.

  ── the cost the row named, removed rather than accepted ──
  The row's other objection was #76: a guide the studio adds shows on /help/
  immediately today, and would have no page until the next website build. Two
  things answer that. The hub still renders an unknown guide inline at runtime
  (see `data-pages` in help.njk), so it is readable the moment the studio
  deploys — it just has no URL of its own until the next build. And this page
  carries help-guide.js, which re-renders THIS guide from the live corpus when
  the studio's copy has moved on, so an EDITED guide is never stale either.

  ── editions (#535) ──
  `entry` is one (edition, guide) pair from src/_data/help.js. A Spanish page
  is written from the studio's `?lang=es` answer, which falls back PER FILE to
  English where the translation has not caught up; such a page is still
  written (a reader following the Spanish hub must never 404), says so above
  the guide, carries `lang="en"` on the body, and is `noindex` and out of the
  sitemap — the English twin is the page to rank. `hreflang` between the twins
  comes from the layout, derived from the build's URL list like every other.
#}
{%- set edition = entry.edition -%}
{%- set guide = entry.guide -%}
{%- set fallback = guide.language != edition.code -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "headline": {{ guide.title | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ guide.description | dump | safe }},
  "author": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
  "publisher": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
  "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}" },
  "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ edition.prefix }}/help/" },
  "isAccessibleForFree": true,
  "articleSection": {{ (guide.topic | t) | dump | safe }},
  "inLanguage": "{{ guide.language }}"
}
</script>

{#- The trail a search result shows instead of the bare URL, and the second
    thing that tells Google /help/ is a section rather than eleven loose pages
    — the first being that every guide links to three siblings (#137's ring). -#}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "{{ site.name }}", "item": "{{ site.url }}{{ '/' | localize }}" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": {{ ('Help' | t) | dump | safe }}, "item": "{{ site.url }}{{ edition.prefix }}/help/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": {{ guide.title | dump | safe }} }
  ]
}
</script>

<header class="help-guide-hero">
  <div class="help-guide-hero-inner">
    <a class="res-back" href="{{ edition.prefix }}/help/">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9.5 3.5L5 8l4.5 4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      {% t %}All guides{% endt %}
    </a>
    <span class="tag">{{ guide.emoji }} {{ guide.topic | t }}</span>
    {#- No dek here. The card's dek is the guide's own opening sentence cut to
        116 characters, so printing it above the guide restates the first
        paragraph a reader is about to read, ellipsis and all. It earns its
        place on a card, where it is choosing between eleven guides, and on
        the <meta name="description">, where it is the search snippet. -#}
    <h1 class="help-guide-h1"{% if fallback %} lang="{{ guide.language }}"{% endif %}>{{ guide.title }}</h1>
  </div>
</header>

{#- `data-guide-hash` is this ONE guide's fingerprint, not the corpus's: the
    hub compares whole corpora because it lists all of them, but a guide page
    only cares whether its own markdown moved. Same "no double render" rule as
    #136 — if the live text hashes the same, nothing is touched.

    The note above the guide is an edition's alone (#535): written on every
    page of a translated edition, hidden where the studio served the file in
    the page's language, and shown — or hidden — again by help-guide.js when
    the live answer says otherwise. The English edition writes none. -#}
<section class="help-guides help-guides-single">
  {%- if edition.code != 'en' %}
  <p class="help-guide-note" id="guideLangNote"{% if not fallback %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ 'This guide is not in {language} yet, so it is shown in English until it is.' | t({ language: edition.own }) }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
  <article class="help-guide" id="guide-{{ guide.slug }}"
           data-slug="{{ guide.slug }}"
           data-guide-hash="{{ guide.hash }}"
           data-guide-source="{{ edition.source }}"{% if fallback %}
           lang="{{ guide.language }}"{% endif %}>
    {{ guide.body | safe }}
  </article>
</section>

{% set others = edition.guides | ring(guide.slug, 3) %}
{% if others.length %}
<section class="help-more">
  <div class="help-more-inner">
    <h2 class="res-more-h">{% t %}More guides{% endt %}</h2>
    <ul class="res-more-list">
      {%- for other in others %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ edition.prefix }}/help/{{ other.slug }}/"{% if other.language != edition.code %} lang="{{ other.language }}"{% endif %}>
          <span class="res-more-title">{{ other.emoji }} {{ other.title }}</span>
          <span class="res-more-dek">{{ other.dek }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="help-dim help-more-all"><a href="{{ edition.prefix }}/help/">{% t %}Search every guide →{% endt %}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="help-support">
  <div class="help-support-inner">
    <span class="tag">{% t %}still stuck{% endt %}</span>
    <h2>{% t %}Ask a person.{% endt %}</h2>
    <p>{% t %}The <strong>Support</strong> pill inside the studio answers in seconds and already knows which workspace you are in. If you would rather write, we read every mail.{% endt %}</p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
    <p class="help-support-alt"><a href="https://studio.prospektor.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% t %}Open the studio ↗{% endt %}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- defer (#170) — see the longer note in src/help.njk. The same reasoning
    reaches this page through help-guide.js, which compares one guide's
    data-guide-hash rather than the whole corpus's: a hash comparison does not
    care when it runs, only that the element it reads is parsed, which is
    exactly what `defer` guarantees. Driven in test/drive.js §7b and §7c(a). -#}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/help-render.js' | asset }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/help-guide.js' | asset }}" defer></script>
